<table style="width:100%">
  <tr>
    <td style="color:#223388; font-size:150%; vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:black; font-weight:600">NIST Atomic Spectra Database Lines Data</span><p>
      <u>Fe XXV</u>: 108 Lines of Data Found<br />
<span style="font-size:larger; font-weight:bold"><i>Z</i> = 26, He isoelectronic sequence</span><span style="font-size=300%">&nbsp;</span></p>
    </td>
    <td style="text-align:right; vertical-align:middle">
<div class='ref'>
<b>Example of how to reference these results:</b><br />

Kramida,&nbsp;A., Ralchenko,&nbsp;Yu., Reader,&nbsp;J., and NIST ASD Team (2024).
  <i>NIST Atomic Spectra Database</i> (ver.&nbsp;5.12),
  [Online]. Available: <span style="color:#0000cc;">https://physics.nist.gov/asd</span>
  [2025, March 22].
  National Institute of Standards and Technology, Gaithersburg, MD.
    DOI: <span style="color:#0000cc;">https://doi.org/10.18434/T4W30F</span>
<br />
<div style="text-align: right; font-size: x-small">
<a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popdef('/cgi-bin/ASD/bibtex.pl?y=2025&amp;m=March&amp;d=22');return true" target="_top">BibTex Citation</a> (new window)
</div>
</div>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td colspan="2">&nbsp;</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td colspan="2" style="color:#655665; font-family: helvetica,arial; font-size:80%"><b><u><i>&lambda;</i> in</u>: <span style="color:darkred">vacuum</span> <span style="color:navy"></span></b></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p>
<table style="background-color:black; width:75%; border-spacing:1px" >
  <tr>
    <td colspan="3" style="color:white; font-size:10pt; width:70%; background-color:#224477; text-align:center">
      <b>Primary data sources</b>
    </td>
    <td rowspan="4">
    </td>
    <td style="white-space:nowrap; color:white; font-size:10pt; background-color:#446655; text-align:center">
      <table style="border:thin hidden;text-align:center;width:100%">
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align:center; white-space:nowrap">Query NIST Bibliographic Databases for</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align:center"><b>Fe  XXV</b> (new window)</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class='brt1'>
      Energy Levels:
    </td>
    <td class='bcn'>
      &nbsp;<a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=21139&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Surzhykov&nbsp;2019</a>, <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=22382&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Drake&nbsp;1985</a>, <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19700&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Si&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2016</a>, <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=11926&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Shirai&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2000</a>&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td class='blf'>
      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;For levels below the ionization limit, the data pertain to the isotope <sup>56</sup>Fe. The 1s<i>n</i>s and 1s<i>n</i>p levels with <i>n</i>&nbsp;&le;&nbsp;7 and the ionization limit are theoretical values compiled by <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=21139&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Surzhykov&nbsp;2019 </a>. Excitation energies of the 1s3d levels have been derived by A. Kramida (unpublished, 2023) from the theoretical ionization energies calculated by <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=22382&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Drake&nbsp;1985 </a> in three steps. First, Drake's values have been scaled to the current values of the fundamental constants (see <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=22677&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Tiesinga&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2021 </a>) and atomic masses (see <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=22713&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Wang&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2021 </a>). Then these adjusted values of ionization energies were subtracted from the ground-state ionization energy calculated by <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=21139&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Surzhykov&nbsp;2019 </a>. Finally, excitation energies of the 1s3d configuration were determined as a straight mean of four values obtained by adding Drake's adjusted 1s3p <sup>1,3</sup>P&deg;<sub>0,1,2</sub> &ndash; 1s3d <i><sup>S</sup>D<sub>J</sub></i> energy intervals to the reference values of the corresponding <sup>1,3</sup>P&deg;<sub>0,1,2</sub> levels from <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=21139&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Surzhykov&nbsp;2019 </a>. The root-mean-square deviation of the four values from the mean, combined in quadrature with the average uncertainty of the reference <sup>1,3</sup>P&deg;<sub>0,1,2</sub> levels, provided a rough estimate of the uncertainies of thus derived 1s3d <i><sup>S</sup>D<sub>J</sub></i> levels. These adjusted values were found to be in good agreement with the values derived in a similar procedure from the many-body perturbation theory (MBPT) calculations of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19700&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Si&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2016 </a> for nuclear charges <i>Z</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;10&ndash;36 (see below). For the 1s4d, 1s5d, 1s6d, 1s<i>n</i>f, and 1s<i>n</i>g (<i>n</i>&nbsp;&le;&nbsp;6) levels, the energies were derived by A. Kramida (unpublished, 2023) from the MBPT calculations of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19700&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Si&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2016 </a>. First, the intervals between the 1s<i>nl</i> <sup>1,3</sup><i>L<sub>J</sub></i> levels (<i>n</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;3&ndash;6, <i>l</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;d, f, g) and the corresponding 1s<i>n</i>p <sup>3</sup>P&deg;<sub>0</sub> levels were calculated either from reference data for <i>Z</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;2&ndash;5 or from <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19700&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Si&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2016 </a> for <i>Z</i>&nbsp;&ge;&nbsp;10. Then these intervals were interpolated along the isoelectronic sequence. The final excitation energies of the 1s<i>nl</i> <sup>1,3</sup><i>L<sub>J</sub></i> levels (<i>n</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;3&ndash;6, <i>l</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;d, f, g) reported here were determined by adding those interpolated intervals to the reference values of the 1s<i>n</i>p <sup>3</sup>P&deg;<sub>0</sub> levels taken from <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=21139&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Surzhykov&nbsp;2019 </a>. Their uncertainies were estimated by adding in quadrature the uncertainties of the reference <sup>3</sup>P&deg;<sub>0</sub> levels to the interpolation uncertainties. Several highly excited Rydberg levels have been determined by A. Kramida (unpublished, 2023) by extrapolations using the Ritz quantum defect expansion formula (see its description in <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=18395&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Kramida&nbsp;2013 </a>). Uncertainties are given here for the separations from the ionization limit. The autoionizing levels, originally from the calculation of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=7187&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Vainshtein&nbsp;&&nbsp;Safronova&nbsp;1985 </a>, are quoted from the compilation of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=11926&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Shirai&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2000 </a>. They are in good agreement with calculations of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19700&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Si&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2016 </a> and those of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19748&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=E');return false">Goryaev&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2017 </a>. The present data set was prepared by A. Kramida for the release of ASD v.5.11 in October, 2023.
    </td>
    <td class='bcn1'>
      <a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popbib('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/Elevbib/make_query.cgi?spectra=Fe%20XXV&amp;method=EL&amp;method=TE&amp;method=ND&amp;method=IP&amp;method=SF&amp;method=QF&amp;order=1');return false"
        onmouseover="self.status='Fe  XXV: bibliography energy levels query';return true;"
        onmouseout="self.status=''; return true;" target="_blank">Fe  XXV Energy Levels</a>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class='brt1'>
      Lines:
    </td>
    <td class='bcn'>
      &nbsp;<a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=11926&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=L');return false">Shirai et al. 2000</a>&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td class='blf'>
      
    </td>
    <td class='bcn1'>
      <a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popbib('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/Elevbib/make_query.cgi?spectra=Fe%20XXV&amp;method=W&amp;method=CL&amp;order=1');return false"
        onmouseover="self.status='Fe  XXV: bibliography wavelengths query';return true;"
        onmouseout="self.status=''; return true;" target="_blank">Fe  XXV Line Wavelengths and Classification</a>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class='brt1'>
      Transition Probabilities:
    </td>
    <td class='bcn'>
      &nbsp;<a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for Fe XXV';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=tp&amp;db_id=5298&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=Fe&amp;spectr_charge=25&amp;type=T');return false">Fuhr et al. 1988</a>&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td class='blf'>
      
    </td>
    <td class='bcn1'>
      <a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popbib('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/Fvalbib/make_query.cgi?spectra=Fe%20XXV&amp;order=1');return false"
        onmouseover="self.status='Fe  XXV: bibliography transition probability query';return true;"
        onmouseout="self.status=''; return true;" target="_blank">Fe  XXV Transition Probabilities</a>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
    <p>
